{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/block/buzz/pulls/5699","id":4265983322,"node_id":"PR_kwDORgXb2s7-Rb1a","html_url":"https://github.com/block/buzz/pull/5699","diff_url":"https://github.com/block/buzz/pull/5699.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/block/buzz/pull/5699.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/block/buzz/issues/5699","number":5699,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"test: add deterministic desktop release smoke","user":{"login":"wesbillman","id":51647,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51647?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman","html_url":"https://github.com/wesbillman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wesbillman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- add `just desktop-release-smoke`, a deterministic desktop correctness/reachability smoke against an ephemeral real local relay\n- seed a 10,000-event dense-second fixture and verify exact event-ID reachability, SHA-256 identity, ordering, duplicate absence, bounded mounted rows, and drained render work\n- isolate Postgres per run, serialize the shared Redis DB, retain phase/relay/Playwright diagnostics, and gate desktop release manifest assembly on the smoke\n\nThis is deliberately **not a performance-regression gate**. CDP and action timing fields are informational only. There is no candidate/baseline comparison or threshold. A future performance lane needs repeated equivalent fixtures, discrete interaction samples, and an explicit comparator/noise policy.\n\nThe diagnostics record the fixture version, row count, wall-clock base timestamp (`fixtureSecond`), expected event-ID hash, observed state, and measurements. Because the created-at floor requires a current timestamp, paired comparison remains disabled.\n\nThe release job runs on an isolated GitHub-hosted runner. The script also guards automatic local runs with a Redis allocation lock. Its remaining direct-PID cleanup and free-port selection race mean it should not be repurposed onto a persistent concurrent shared runner without first hardening process-group cleanup and port reservation.\n\n### Related issue\n\nN/A\n\n### Testing\n\n- `pnpm --dir desktop typecheck`\n- focused real-local-relay release smoke passed after adversarial review fixes\n- full pre-push hook suite passed on `6da18868d15aef95743d8a3cc8bab472a69e9f63`\n- full 10,000-event scenario reached 10,000/10,000 exact IDs with matching SHA-256, 199 continuation requests, and 95 mounted rows in about 4.4 minutes\n- reduced-row review run passed in 18.4 seconds\n","created_at":"2026-08-12T21:01:53Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T21:01:54Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cac034cc9eda04ea770ca0de4bb04f37cb59eeac","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/block/buzz/pulls/5699/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/block/buzz/pulls/5699/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/block/buzz/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/block/buzz/issues/5699/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/block/buzz/statuses/6da18868d15aef95743d8a3cc8bab472a69e9f63","head":{"label":"block:carl/desktop-release-smoke","ref":"carl/